<title>USA: Minn. governor pushes for S&amp;P upgrade to AAA.</title>
<headline>Minn. governor pushes for S&amp;P upgrade to AAA.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minnesota Gov. Arne Carlson went to New York Monday to push for a rating upgrade to AAA from Standard &amp; Poor's Corp, a spokesman for the governor said.</p>
<p>Brian Dietz said Carlson was to present perameters of the state's upcoming two-year budget to rating analysts, as well as assurances the state is &quot;on the right track&quot; financially. Minnesota is currently rated AA-plus with a positive outlook by Standard &amp; Poor's. The state already has AAA grades from Moody's Investors Service Inc and Fitch Investor's</p>
<p>Service Inc.</p>
<p>    ((--Karen Pierog, 312-408-8647)) (c) Reuters Limited 1997</p>
